        "reviewed_sha": "b2b349f3607b14633db66340b2e643563a868ddf",
        "evidence": "S↔L: the ref resolves to the library lean/QOU/Braiding/hecke_mass_trace.lean:88, which is self-assuming. Both claims are class fields (`claim_cat_mass_eq_norm_trace`, `claim_trace_decomposition`, l.70-82) and are returned as a pair, with `cat_mass` and `norm` free. The sibling .lean differs: it has no `hecke_mass_trace`, it *defines* the mass as |markovTrace| (lean:127-128), the decomposition is a structure field (l.66-67, 108), and it adds ℝ positivity variants. S↔P: steps 1-4 (prf:1-20) are assertions about τ (\"exact and monoidal … norm preservation\") rather than an argument. \"|·|\" on the Laurent ring R is never defined, which is the point the sibling's own two-tier note raises (lean:16-21). The decomposition needs Φ_mass = Φ^desc + ΣΦ^trans_i, which is asserted (\"τ … preserves the idempotent splitting\", prf:27-28), not shown. Quantum Schur–Weyl gives End_{U_q}(V^⊗n) as a quotient of H_n (TL), not H_n itself (prf:10-11).",
        "notes": "Genuine side-by-side review (statement / narrative proof / Lean), main b2b349f36; findings in issue #8025. Route: exposition"
      }
